    "## 3.X Feature scaling\n",
    "\n",
    "To prepare the features for moding, we standardize them using **Scikit-Learn's StandardScaler**. This transforms the features to have a mean of 0 and a standard deviation of 1.\n",
    "\n",
    "The scaling is done due to Logistic Regression is sensitive to the scale of input features. Features with larger numeric ranges could otherwise dominate the model's coefficients.\n",
    "\n",
    "Scaler is fitted strictly on the training set **X_train** to learn its mean and variance. These values are then applied to the test set **X_test**, ensuring no information from the testing data leaks into the training process."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 101,
   "id": "5849b3d83213e2bb",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-10-08T14:11:46.954943100Z",
     "start_time": "2026-10-08T14:11:46.433033600Z"
    }
   },
